{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Page Network AI Interface.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Page Network AI Interface.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"multi page network ai interface multi page network ai interface","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Page Network AI Interface.md","fileName":"Multi-Page Network AI Interface.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Multi-Page Network AI Interface","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 18:30\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Network AI Application Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Network AI Application Architecture","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Page Network AI Interface.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Page Network AI Interface.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"multi page network ai interface multi page network ai interface","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Page Network AI Interface.md","fileName":"Multi-Page Network AI Interface.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Multi-Page Network AI Interface","heading":"Multi-Page Network AI Interface","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A multi-page network AI interface separates operational views such as a dashboard and a configuration form while keeping navigation consistent. Wrapping each page in a function lets a main application choose what to render without executing every page's code on import.\n\nAs the application grows, pages, reusable components, utilities, data, secrets, and documentation should occupy distinct folders. This structure makes ownership and testing clearer and prevents one script from mixing UI state, model calls, data access, and rendering. Navigation is therefore an architectural boundary, not just a visual menu.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Network AI Applica